Print a tree of documentation paths

Builds a directory-like tree from all page paths stored in the documentation database.

Examples:
  docs_tree
  docs_tree {"depth": 2}
  docs_tree {"filter": "sdk"}

Each line shows one path segment. A line whose path is a page also shows the page's title, after " - ". For example, `docs_tree {"filter": "rust"}` prints:

  reference
  ┗━━ sdk - SDKs
      ┗━━ rust - Rust SDK
          ┣━━ example - Rust SDK tutorial, times10 function
          ┣━━ instrumentation - Rust instrumentation
          ┗━━ legacy_instrumentation - Legacy Rust instrumentation

To get the path of a page, join the segments of its parent lines and its own line, from the top level down, with "/", for example reference/sdk/rust/example. `docs_show` accepts this path.

With `json`, the tree prints as one JSON object, {"children": [node, ...]}. Each node has name, the last segment of its path, and path. A node has title when it is a page, and then `docs_show` accepts its path. A node has children, sorted by name, when it has child nodes that `depth` did not remove. When no page matches, the output is {"children": []}.
